^[chapter/05/sections][
  s01: <
    handle: "custom-boof/01"
    type: "custom-boof"
    excerpt: "The counting room was calm the way a held breath is calm. Boof followed a faint melody along the floor-crack — the Fool’s Song — not a lure this time, a diagnostic. Two slips hung over the open ledger. Each was a rece..."
    route: ^[chapter/05/s01]{open}
  >
  s02: <
    handle: "custom-song/02"
    type: "custom-song"
    excerpt: "The song did not say come closer. It named the fracture: one receipt for a harvest that arrived, one receipt for a harvest that was only sealed. Melody made the disagreement audible without forcing a false fix."
    handles: ["song-verse"]
    route: ^[chapter/05/s02]{open}
  >
  s03: <
    handle: "custom-fool/03"
    type: "custom-fool"
    excerpt: "\"You hear it, don’t you, Boof?\" The Fool’s voice sang with the crack. \"This is my song. It is also the ledger's. A quiet rift is still a rift.\""
    route: ^[chapter/05/s03]{open}
  >
